1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
With Asta's help, Fuegolion subdued the insane mage who had let loose an undead army upon the capital in his search for revenge.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I get that you wanted people to take you seriously, but I don't understand why you had to do it like this.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Magic?

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Allow me to thank you for your service, Magic Knights.

8
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,000
What the...

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Caught off guard by a spatial magic spell, the elite members of the Magic Knights were pulled from the attack's aftermath and transported far from the capital.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
I knew there was a strong spatial magic user working with them, but even so...

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
To do this, transporting us all would require great skill.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Spatial magic again, eh?

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Very well. Maybe now we'll get to the bottom of this.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Fuegolion Vermillion, captain of the Crimson Lion Kings, was himself warped away to a mysterious realm.

15
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
It's you!

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Meanwhile, having avoided the spatial ambush that ensnared his colleagues, Yuno battled a powerful witch who used her Ash curse magic to leave him in a state of total sensory deprivation.

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,000
But then...

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
I'm not done!

19
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
I'm not done!

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
There's just one very important thing to know about me.

21
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The truth is...

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
I would rather give my life than lose!

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Win spirit magic!

24
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Silk scratch!

25
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
boşver!

26
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Yes ho!

27
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Maybe

28
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,880
What's wrong with all Rose?

29
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,420
Let's just rest him

30
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:45,920
Why?

31
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:46,440
Support me

32
00:02:46,440 --> 00:03:00,640
Stop

33
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:20,100
ifornia

34
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,460
I'm all over.

35
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,340
My shell.

36
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:04,420
Shell!

37
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:06,860
Wonderful!

38
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:07,840
Yes!

39
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:10,080
This little shortcake knows how to eat.

40
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,760
It's a chef's trade come true!

41
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,460
Keep going.

42
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,240
Savor every last bite.

43
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,460
Yes, eat it all!

44
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,720
The entire capital's under siege,

45
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:22,320
and this is what they care about?

46
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,580
You just say when you're ready for more,

47
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,380
and I'll make you seconds, even thirds!

48
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:26,960
Hooray!

49
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,820
What now?

50
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:39,880
A witch?

51
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:41,600
We're under attack!

52
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:44,220
What the hell do you think we've been trying to tell you?

53
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:45,320
Please, chef!

54
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:46,200
It's time to bail!

55
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:47,740
Run for it, shortcake!

56
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,420
My mana!

57
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,020
It's draining!

58
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,420
I need to steal some more!

59
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,640
What are you doing, shortcake?

60
00:04:58,760 --> 00:04:59,460
Just run!

61
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:01,840
That little girl, saturated with mana!

62
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:03,860
She's greasy with the stuff!

63
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:09,980
I need every last drop of it!

64
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:10,840
Give it to me!

65
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,420
I want it!

66
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,300
If you would!

67
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,280
Wait, you don't mean...

68
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,220
Not my lunch!

69
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:20,780
Not my lunch!

70
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,420
No way, lady!

71
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:28,700
Now give it to me!

72
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,660
I need mana!

73
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:40,240
I can still sense her mana.

74
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,700
That witch has to be alive somewhere.

75
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:48,120
I won't last much longer.

76
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,240
What?

77
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,580
That's a massive surge of magic!

78
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:58,300
Relinquish it to me!

79
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:07,900
I told you no.

80
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:13,740
And when I say no, I mean no.

81
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:14,440
I mean no.

82
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:24,580
This is ridiculous!

83
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,100
You won't think so for long.

84
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:28,980
Cotton creation magic!

85
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,240
Strike of the sleeping sheep!

86
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:43,840
That was awesome!

87
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:47,200
Well, you see that?

88
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,960
My cooking gave the little shortcake's magic power

89
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,080
the boost it needed to defeat the witch!

90
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:53,180
Seriously?

91
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,720
Chef, sir?

92
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:57,220
I'll work with you for as long as I live!

93
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,840
You saved us with your feast!

94
00:06:58,880 --> 00:06:59,860
It was nothing.

95
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:03,040
I don't care who you are.

96
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,920
Nobody ever lays a hand on my food.

97
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,080
Your patronage is not wanted here!

98
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:15,560
What?

99
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:22,380
Please tell me I'm beautiful.

100
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:29,720
My dear Eliza.

101
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:30,540
Yes?

102
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,240
I'll always love you.

103
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,460
Young or old.

104
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:34,800
And I love you.

105
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:44,560
Eliza!

106
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,000
My dearest!

107
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,060
My dearest!

108
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:55,040
My dearest!

109
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:05,620
Young Meg!

110
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,780
Ha!

111
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,020
Wag!

112
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,600
Amelia!

113
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:12,740
Her.

114
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:12,900
My dearest!

115
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:13,240
Her.

116
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:13,700
My dearest!

117
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:14,040
Her.

118
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:14,060
Hi!

119
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:19,520
A child?

120
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,980
That outrageously powerful burst of magic.

121
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:28,480
Was that her?

122
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,780
She's wearing a black bull's robe.

123
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,100
It must have been.

124
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,380
You saved my boy!

125
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,280
Oh, uh, here.

126
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:41,420
I don't get it, but sure.

127
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:45,100
Thank you so...

128
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:55,520
My princely thank you, sustenance!

129
00:08:57,660 --> 00:09:01,840
Um, I owe you a tremendous debt, noble sir.

130
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:08,960
Could you tell me what...

131
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,680
A short wig?

132
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,920
Oh, yeah, they're great!

133
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,600
You can try one if you want to.

134
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,100
Wait, no, no, no, no.

135
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,180
That's not it.

136
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:15,640
I'm...

137
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,200
Min...

138
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,640
Could you tell me what your name is?

139
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,800
I mean, don't get me wrong.

140
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,660
You can have one, but I know what a short wig is.

141
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:22,800
Here comes the crash.

142
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:23,740
I mean, I know about all sorts of meat.

143
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,220
That magic took a serious toll on my body.

144
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,360
It used up a ton of mana.

145
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:32,880
I need practice.

146
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,600
Gotta learn to be more efficient.

147
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,200
Oh, no, no, no, no!

148
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,260
Look out!

149
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:42,460
Saved you!

150
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:42,980
Aah!

151
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,140
Aah!

152
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:44,560
Aah!

153
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:46,380
Saved you!

154
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:56,140
I guess I'll just need this to be on the way.

155
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:06,300
What is that infernal racket out there?

156
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:08,640
Will you order them to quiet down?

157
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,020
Don't they know it's my nap time?

158
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:13,360
I'll look into it, sire.

159
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:21,280
Is it him?

160
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,760
It's about time he made his return.

161
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,900
You forever want a place in our hearts, little shortcake.

162
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:35,080
Just stop on by whenever you're hungry, day or night.

163
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:37,060
We'll feed you until you're ready to pop.

164
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:37,960
Yay!

165
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,920
You evil bastard!

166
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:47,420
Tell me where you sent my brother!

167
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:57,920
He's just toying with you.

168
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,740
He wasn't the one who cast this spatial magic spell.

169
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,020
But the pinpoint accuracy of it.

170
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:06,020
No one could pull that off unless they were close to their target.

171
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:10,020
They're hiding nearby.

172
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:26,340
Asta?

173
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:40,480
He was hiding beneath the pile of corpses?

174
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,840
Nice observation skills.

175
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:48,460
I had a feeling you'd suss out my magical transformations.

176
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:52,160
But I couldn't even get past you with a shabby putrescent disguise.

177
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,940
You really are quite the animal.

178
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:56,700
Hmm.

179
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:00,260
Regardless, it's already over now.

180
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:00,980
Over?

181
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:02,580
What is?

182
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:12,380
APS

183
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:20,660
Ha-ha.

184
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:28,100
AHHHHHHHHHHH!

185
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,360
OHH!!!

186
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,360
NOOOOO!!!

187
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:40,800
귀 celto!!

188
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,860
Fya'd..

189
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:49,140
But how...?

190
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:54,140
How can someone be that strong? That's just... insane!

191
00:12:58,140 --> 00:13:00,140
They... his arm...

192
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:06,140
This can't be... No...

193
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:28,140
You can't die... Fuegoleon... No... Not my brother... He would never lose... He'd never lose... NEVER!

194
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:40,140
It's Captain Fuegoleon's grimoire! Wait, if his grimoire's still intact then... He's not dead yet! We have to stop the bleeding!

195
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:47,140
Impossible... There's no way... If only Mimosa were here, she could fix this...

196
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:59,140
Leopold! Your brother's grimoire is starting to disintegrate! Snap out of it! I need your help!

197
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,140
My brother...

198
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:05,140
Leopold! Are you just going to let your brother die?

199
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:10,140
Well, Magic Knight, not so sure of yourself anymore now, are you?

200
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,140
Pull it together!

201
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:23,140
He still has a reserve of magic power!

202
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,140
Ah!

203
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:44,140
Perhaps you could have become a great man if you had gone down a different path. This is where the lack of a just heart has led you.

204
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:51,140
I lack a just heart, do I? Well, I have to tell you, the way I live my life, my heart's done just right by me!

205
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:55,140
Looks like you'll have to save your preaching for the afterlife, Captain!

206
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:59,140
You've fulfilled your purpose here.

207
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:01,140
Huh?

208
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:04,140
Take your leave, Radies, before the other knights arrive.

209
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:13,140
No way! Not yet!

210
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:14,140
Huh?

211
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:26,140
It's little Oster, right? Don't worry, I promise to kill you soon enough! And make a plaything of your corpse! Something we can both look forward to, you brat!

212
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,140
Ah!

213
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,140
Yeah!

214
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:30,140
Ah!

215
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,140
Asta!

216
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:37,140
I'm not close enough. I'll never make it!

217
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:42,140
Just let him go!

218
00:15:43,140 --> 00:15:45,140
He's losing too much blood! He has to stop!

219
00:15:45,140 --> 00:15:46,140
I can do this!

220
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:50,140
Remember what Captain Foigolion told you? Stay calm and think!

221
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:55,140
There must be some way I can stop him! I just have to figure out what it is!

222
00:15:57,140 --> 00:16:01,140
Spatial magic is still magic! And I've still got my sword!

223
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:05,140
I'm gonna hack that spell to pieces!

224
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,140
What the hell?

225
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:09,140
The hell?

226
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:20,140
That hurts! You're gonna pay for that, you little wretch!

227
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,140
Unfortunate.

228
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:30,140
You're whining about a little cut after the pain you've caused!

229
00:16:31,140 --> 00:16:34,140
You want pain? I'll give you pain!

230
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:40,140
You torture innocent people and laugh the whole time!

231
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:44,140
Stop it!

232
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:51,140
Those poor innocents you're so worried about? That only proves how weak they are!

233
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:56,140
It's just the natural order! The weaker mage will always succumb to the one with greater power!

234
00:16:56,140 --> 00:17:02,140
And you... you were born to die, you magic-efficient swine!

235
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:07,140
The natural order, huh?

236
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:11,140
Then what do you call this?

237
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:14,140
That's right.

238
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:19,140
Maybe I don't have any magic, but I'm still the strongest one here!

239
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:23,140
And I'll prove it to everyone when I become the Wizard King!

240
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:27,140
Hey, Voltos! I could use a little help here!

241
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:31,140
Hmph. I've already done everything I can.

242
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:34,140
Anti-magic. It's trickier than I expected.

243
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:38,140
Seems like the smartest plan of action is to take care of him first.

244
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:51,140
He's gathering magic power. But for what?

245
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:55,140
Is he going to attack through a spatial portal?

246
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:57,140
Is he going to attack through a spatial portal?

247
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:59,140
Asta! Behind you!

248
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:01,140
Too late.

249
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:14,140
Being upset won't help us.

250
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:18,140
Always remember to stay calm. Right, brother?

251
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:21,140
Let's go, Asta!

252
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:23,140
Please be careful!

253
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,140
Please be careful!

254
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,140
So what should I do?

255
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,140
I can't afford to lose Radies just yet.

256
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:42,140
Get away from me!

257
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:44,140
Stay back!

258
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:45,140
Get away, dammit!

259
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:47,140
How pitiful.

260
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:53,140
I come here after receiving word from the Master.

261
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:58,140
Only to arrive and find you fighting this pitiful indeed.

262
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,140
Indeed.

263
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:25,140
This magic. I've never felt anything so piercingly cold.

264
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:27,140
So now there's five of them?

265
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:30,140
This curse I've got on me.

266
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,140
None of these scrapes and scratches will stop bleeding.

267
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:37,140
I'm going to be in serious trouble if I lose any more blood.

268
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:42,140
I don't remember putting out the call for any extra help!

269
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,140
Really? You might want to try thanking us.

270
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:48,140
You know what would have happened to you if we hadn't shown up to bail you out?

271
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:52,140
